{
 "updated": "2026-11-17 00:53 PT",
 "status": "First 16k results (one seed, eval_size 184). The current recipe reaches the dense-LoRA reference's 100-step loss with 1.9x fewer training FLOPs (1.3x if every task must reach its own reference level, at the 70-step level); its transient memory is 1.24x dense LoRA's, so it saves no memory under activation checkpointing. The first gold-aware stochastic-keep arms (0.08-0.12x dense per step) fall well short of the reference loss. About 25 more runs are in progress on jsteinhardt, Beaker and Lambda.",
 "setup": [
  "Each method trains with its own forward, optimiser and real LR schedule on the same first batches of the pool (16 rows/step, 2 GPUs).",
  "At fixed steps the dense forward (full context, no dropping, adapters on) is scored on held-out rows from the CTC-suite eval files: teacher-forced answer CE, 16 rows per task and length (4k, 8k, 16k) except reorder at 16k, where only 8 eval rows fit in 16,384 tokens; eval_size 184.",
  "Score = training FLOPs the dense reference needs to reach a loss level divided by the FLOPs the method needs to reach the same level, on the mean loss and on the worst task. Peak GPU memory is logged per step.",
  "One iteration is under 15 minutes. Every 2-3 hours the most promising methods get a larger FLOP-matched training run with generation-graded evals.",
  "Data caveats: the 16k training cells use fewer documents per row than the eval (contradiction 324 vs 379, outlier 96 vs 111, reorder 90 vs 116) so rows fit in 16,384 tokens; the 16k held-out rows are the short tail of the eval rung (70, 303, 8 and 497 of 500 rows fit for contradiction, outlier, reorder, qdmatch_nq). About 46% of the documents in a qdmatch_nq held-out row also occur in training rows (no gold overlap, no prompt overlap).",
  "Memory is reported as the step's transient (peak minus the weights and optimizer state held before the step), since under activation checkpointing the absolute peak is dominated by the fixed part."
 ],
 "log": [
  {
   "t": "11-17 00:40",
   "text": "Lambda (2 x A100 per run) and Beaker (2 x H100 per run) staged and verified: step-0 loss matches Berkeley. Six Beaker jobs launched (LR and rows-per-step sweeps, dense-LoRA reference LR check, keep ladder down to 2% / 1%)."
  },
  {
   "t": "11-17 00:55",
   "text": "References done: dense full FT 0.135 and dense LoRA 0.131 held-out CE at step 100; recipe 0.125 at step 200 for 0.22x dense per step. Reorder dominates the mean loss (about 0.33 for all three; the other tasks 0.04-0.11)."
  },
  {
   "t": "11-17 00:05",
   "text": "CPT search: a usable token-exit CPT base (dropstruct, tokens leave from block 8, 64M CPT tokens) and its dense-CPT control exist and are staged; the 1B-token FFN-drop CPT base was deleted on 10-30."
  },
  {
   "t": "11-17 00:25",
   "text": "Pool mtb16k and held-out v2 final after one rebuild (16k cells regenerated with fewer documents so rows fit in 16,384 tokens). References and baselines launched on 6 GPUs; all 8 preemptive_high GPUs in use."
  },
  {
   "t": "11-16 23:45",
   "text": "Seven idea agents started (no-grad prefix + early cuts, gold-aware stochastic keep, early-layer loss selection, detached context, FLOP-aware row sampling, FFN skip for context tokens, token-drop CPT base search). Staging agents started for Lambda and Beaker."
  },
  {
   "t": "11-16 23:10",
   "text": "Loop requested: tasks switched to contradiction, outlier, reorder, qdmatch_nq at 4k-16k; target 10-20x FLOPs and 5-10x less peak memory."
  }
